-sampler!\n4473:(defn- d1-persist-and-check-fixture!\n4543:         :spot-checks (when spot-check? (d1-spot-check-refusals! input))})\n4547:(deftest test-d1-persisted-per-fixture-static-gate\n4550:        run (fresh-admission-run :d1-r7-static)\n4551:        dir (str \"target/test-d1-r7-\" (random-uuid))]\n4553:      (let [result (d1-persist-and-check-fixture! dir run fixture)]\n4563:(deftest test-d1-persisted-another-fixture-static-gate\n4565:        run (fresh-admission-run :d1-r7-second)\n4566:        dir (str \"target/test-d1-r7-second-\" (random-uuid))]\n4568:      (let [result (d1-persist-and-check-fixture! dir run fixture)]\n4577:(defn- d1-corpus-batch!\n4586:  ([outcomes-file store-dir] (d1-corpus-batch! outcomes-file store-dir nil))\n4602:           run (fresh-admission-run :d1-r8-corpus)\n4603:           sampler (d1-heap-sampler! 5)\n4608:                                      before-bytes (d1-store-bytes store-dir)\n4612:                                    (let [checked (d1-persist-and-check-fixture!\n4618:                                                   :storage-bytes (- (d1-store-bytes store-dir) before-bytes)\n4624:                                      (println \"d1-corpus\" id :pass (:elapsed-ms outcome) \"ms\"\n4641:                                        (println \"d1-corpus\" id :refused (:stage outcome)\n4654:        :store-bytes (d1-store-bytes store-dir)\n4659:(deftest test-d1-corpus-static-gates\n4669:        run-config-file (io/file \"target/d1-corpus-run.edn\")\n4685:                          (str \"target/test-d1-corpus-\" (random-uuid) \".edn\"))\n4687:                      (str \"target/test-d1-corpus-store-\" (random-uuid)))\n4695:      (let [batch (d1-corpus-batch! outcomes-file store-dir\n4722:          (let [rest-batch (d1-corpus-batch! outcomes-file store-dir {:limit 1})]\nCreated-GMT: 2026-11-11 13:40:00 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-11 20:40:00 +0700\nCoding-Agent: muse\nSession-ID: 7db9b5cc-3472-4c31-9657-1b41aaa76ae3\n\n# cc3 bounded run declaration v2 — NEW versioned run (astra r4 ruling (c))\n\nThis declaration is written BEFORE the v2 measurement run, per design\n§6.3 and astra's r4 exceedance ruling (c). It creates a NEW, explicitly\nversioned bounded run. It does not amend, re-scope, or relabel the\nsuperseded run (see §5).\n\n## 1. Pinned corpus, revision, host, and JVM settings\n\n| Item | Pinned value |\n|---|---|\n| Worktree / branch | `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3`, branch `cc3-lowering-provenance` |\n| Base revision | `ced9f2c2bdb43ab4a416b4ab408c76eb29245764` plus the uncommitted cc3 diff (ten tracked files, +1651/−98 at r6 delivery: the eight cc3 files plus the two F7 diagnostic scripts `test/d2_wedge_min_repro.clj` / `test/d2_wedge_probe2.clj`, which the measurement script does not load; latte oracle test file further changed in r5 for F2 caller threading — behaviour-neutral for this fixture's compiled content). Exact pin: see the digest rows below and §6. |\n| Fixture (the whole corpus of this run) | `{:id :cc3-binding :call '(latte-kernel.utils/vectorn? [1 2 3] 2)}` admitted through `kernel-compile`, bound through `cc3-oracle-binding` |\n| Upstream oracle revision | latte-kernel `86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279` (pinned in `deps.edn` `:test` alias) |\n| Compiler base recorded by the evidence harness | `7dc18478` |\n| Host | Darwin 25.6.0 arm64, Apple M1 Pro, 17,179,869,184 B RAM |\n| JVM | OpenJDK 17.0.18+0 (Homebrew, 64-Bit Server VM, mixed mode) |\n| Clojure | Clojure CLI 1.12.4.1602; no explicit `-Xmx` (JVM default max heap). JVM stack: **corrected in r6 (V2)** — the v2 (r5) measured command (§4 as originally written) activated ONLY the `:f6` alias, which supplied `:extra-paths [\"test\"]` and the latte-kernel `:extra-deps` and NO `:jvm-opts`; the project `:test` alias was NOT activated, so its `-Xss64m` (`deps.edn:52`) and its test-runner main-opts were NOT in effect for the v2 run. The v2 samples therefore stand as measured under the JVM default thread stack. The v2.1 declared command (§4, r6 revision) supplies `-Xss64m` explicitly through `:f6`'s own `:jvm-opts [\"-Xss64m\"]`, and the v2.1 results in §6 were measured under exactly that declared command. `-Xss64m` is declared for parity with the `:test` stack policy and headroom, not because the v2 ceilings depended on it: the v2 samples already met every ceiling without it. |\n| Measurement script | `collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-cc3-f6-measure.clj` (in-repo, r5 revision: maximum-based rule, compiled-inclusive holder) |\n| Measured patch pin (SHA-256) | `git diff` (ten tracked files listed in §6) = `05076f51add1a5b5285c62c6b85c7eb8875d7c2780a7b33613e46742a250887d` (computed 2026-11-11 after the final r6 code edit; reproduce with `git diff \\| shasum -a 256` in this worktree) |\n| Measurement script pin (SHA-256) | `shasum -a 256 collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-cc3-f6-measure.clj` = `345b432dace388ce20bb463d2241c650b400b644b5194cd0ddae1a3fb42b37c8` |\n\n## 2. Retained object set and maximum simultaneous retention\n\nThe retained set for one fixture, all held simultaneously by one local\nholder (never a global Var), is:\n\n- the **compiled input**: the `kernel-compile` result (compiled AST,\n  stamped AST, site table, retained `:admission-origin`);\n- the **binding**: `cc3-oracle-binding` result (C1 tree, rows, marked\n  and eligible occurrence sets, site→key binding);\n- the **reconstruction evidence**: the binding's stamped tree/rows,\n  stamped marked/eligible sets, site correspondence map, and stamped\n  paths — i.e. everything needed to reconstruct and verify each bound\n  key from the retained compilation;\n- the lowered images: `linearize/project-rows` output plus\n  `derive/stack-image` and `derive/register-image`;\n- the provenance relation (schema-1 map over admission/root and the\n  semantic, stack, and register call-provenance) and, in the pipeline\n  variant, its durable record in a file-backed content store.\n\nTwo holder variants are measured: **binding-only** (binding, lowered\nimages, relation, reconstruction evidence — the compiled input is\nreleased after binding) and **compiled-inclusive** (the same set plus\nthe retained compiled input). The compiled-inclusive variant is the\nacceptance variant; the binding-only variant is reported for\ncomparison and is NOT the acceptance holder.\n\n**Maximum simultaneously retained fixtures: 1.** Every retained and\npeak measurement holds exactly one fixture's retained set at a time;\nthe previous holder is released (and GC-pinned) before the next\nrepetition builds a new one.\n\n## 3. Ceilings (separate, finite, pilot-justified)\n\nPilot measurements (superseded run, r4, warm JVM, same host/JVM):\nbinding-only retained samples 7,960,192 / 7,921,728 / 8,044,024 B\n(median 7,960,192 B, **maximum 8,044,024 B**); compiled-inclusive\nsamples 9,008,912 / 8,939,024 / 8,826,416 B (median 8,939,024 B,\n**maximum 9,008,912 B**); serialized rows 293,924 B; serialized\nrelation 802,260 B; peak used heap 292,720,240 B (GC-pinned baseline\n38,967,336 B); pipeline elapsed 1,727 ms.\n\n| Ceiling | v2 bound | Justification / headroom over pilot |\n|---|---|---|\n| Storage, per artifact (serialized canonical bytes) | **2,000,000 B** | Kept from r2. Pilot rows 293,924 B (6.8× headroom), relation 802,260 B (2.5× headroom). |\n| Storage, aggregate retained serialized set (rows + relation + durable record, 1 fixture) | **4,000,000 B** | Pilot rows+relation = 1,096,184 B; the durable record is a small map over the same data. 4,000,000 B is ≥3.6× the pilot partial sum, leaving room for the record while staying finite. |\n| Retained memory, aggregate (1 fixture, compiled-inclusive holder) | **12,000,000 B** | Set ABOVE the pilot compiled-inclusive **maximum** 9,008,912 B by 2,991,088 B (**+33.2% headroom**; +34.2% over the 8,939,024 B median; +49.2% over the binding-only maximum 8,044,024 B). Pilot repetition spread was ~2% (8,826,416–9,008,912 B), so 33% covers GC-delta noise, the longer r5 run-scope strings (tens of bytes), and host jitter on this machine class, without being an order-of-magnitude loosening. The floor is the measured maximum, per ruling (c): a ceiling at or below 9,008,912 B would declare a run already known to exceed it. |\n| Peak heap (absolute used heap during the pipeline) | **1,073,741,824 B (1 GiB)** | Kept from r2. Pilot peak 292,720,240 B is 27.3% of this ceiling (3.67× headroom); the figure is absolute used heap (baseline + harness + transients), so the margin absorbs sampler/baseline variance. |\n| Time, per pipeline repetition (compile → persistence → both tagged lanes) | **10,000 ms** | Kept from r2. Pilot 1,727 ms gives 5.8× headroom; warm-JVM figure, cold-JVM limits are stated in §4. |\n| Guest instructions / trace records per C lane | **4,000,000 / 1,000,000** | Restated from the r1 record, NOT raised. |\n\n## 4. Exact reproducible measurement procedure\n\nScript: `collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-cc3-f6-measure.clj`\n(r5 revision). Run from the worktree root:\n\n```\nclojure -Sdeps '{:aliases {:f6 {:extra-paths [\"test\"] :jvm-opts [\"-Xss64m\"] :extra-deps {latte-kernel/latte-kernel {:git/url \"https://github.com/latte-central/latte-kernel\" :git/sha \"86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279\"}}}}}' -M:f6 collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-cc3-f6-measure.clj\n```\n\n(Settings actually in effect, r6-corrected: the `:f6` alias defined\ninline by `-Sdeps` supplies everything — `:extra-paths [\"test\"]` puts\nthe oracle test namespace on the classpath, `:jvm-opts [\"-Xss64m\"]`\nsets the thread stack (added in the r6 revision of this command; the\nv2 run used the same command WITHOUT `:jvm-opts`, i.e. the JVM\ndefault stack — see §1), and `:extra-deps` pins latte-kernel. The\nproject's `:test` alias is NOT activated: its `-Xss64m`\n(`deps.edn:52`) and test-runner main opts play no part. The\nlatte-kernel git dependency is named explicitly because the `:test`\nalias, which normally carries it, also carries the test-runner main\nopts; the git checkout is already cached locally. Verdicts are read\nfrom the script's printed `:under-ceilings-v2` map, computed by the\nmaximum rule below. The v2.1 results under this exact declared\ncommand are recorded in §6.)\n\nProcedure, in order:\n\n1. **Warmup**: build one retained structure and one full pipeline\n   pass, DISCARD both, GC-pin. Class loading / JIT are charged to the\n   warmup, not to measured repetitions.\n2. **Retained memory**: 5 repetitions per holder variant\n   (binding-only, then compiled-inclusive). Each repetition builds a\n   fresh holder held only by a local, samples GC-pinned used heap\n   (`System/gc()`, 50 ms, `System/gc()`, then\n   `Runtime.totalMemory − freeMemory`) before and after, uses\n   `System/identityHashCode` on the holder AFTER the second sample so\n   it cannot be collected early, and releases it on return. ALL 5\n   samples per variant are recorded.\n3. **Peak / pipeline**: 3 pipeline repetitions. A sampler thread\n   records used heap every 2 ms across lowering → binding /\n   projection / derives → actual serialization\n   (`dao.jing/canonical-bytes`) → durable persistence\n   (`dao.jing/materialize!` of relation and record into a file-backed\n   `yin.repl.store`, closed) → tagged execution (both C lanes must\n   reach `:completed`). Peak, per-repetition elapsed time, and\n   serialized byte counts are recorded per repetition.\n4. **Pass/fail is MAXIMUM-based** (r5 F6 fix): a ceiling is met only\n   if the MAXIMUM observed value is at or under it — retained memory:\n   max of the 5 compiled-inclusive samples ≤ 12,000,000 B (the\n   binding-only samples are reported, and also max-checked against\n   the same aggregate ceiling for information); storage: max per\n   artifact and max aggregate ≤ their ceilings; peak heap: max peak\n   over the 3 repetitions ≤ 1 GiB; time: max elapsed ≤ 10,000 ms.\n   Any single sample over its ceiling = EXCEEDED. Medians are\n   printed for information only and never establish compliance.\n\nSampling limitations (named, not hidden): retained and peak figures\nare process-wide JVM used-heap values, not an object-graph census;\n`System/gc()` is a hint the JVM honored observably here, not a\nguarantee; 2 ms peak sampling can miss sub-2 ms transients; figures\nare comparable only on this host/JVM class and only for the named\nholder scope; times are warm-JVM (the discarded warmup precedes all\nmeasured repetitions).\n\n## 5. Superseded run: failed status preserved\n\nThe r2/r4 bounded run (8,000,000 B aggregate retained ceiling,\nmedian-based accounting in its r4 record) **FAILED and remains\nfailed**. Its exceedances, restated with maximum-based accounting:\n\n- compiled-inclusive holder: samples 9,008,912 / 8,939,024 /\n  8,826,416 B — every sample over the 8,000,000 B ceiling.\n  **EXCEEDED.**\n- binding-only holder: samples 7,960,192 / 7,921,728 / 8,044,024 B —\n  the 8,044,024 B sample is over the 8,000,000 B ceiling, so under\n  the corrected maximum rule this holder is **EXCEEDED** too (its r4\n  \"under (99.5%)\" median label is corrected in r5; the samples\n  themselves are unchanged).\n\nNothing in this v2 declaration relabels that run successful, raises\nits ceiling retroactively, or shrinks its fixture. The v2 run below\nis a separate, new run under the ceilings in §3; its results are\nrecorded in the r5 findings, not back-written into the superseded\nrun's record.\n\n## 6. Exact pin and v2.1 re-measurement under the corrected declared settings (r6, V2)\n\nPin (computed 2026-11-11 after the final r6 code edit; nothing in\nthe measured patch changed afterwards — the digest was re-verified\nidentical after the diagnostic-script runs and lint):\n\n- Ten-file tracked diff (`git diff`, +1651/−98):\n  `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`,\n  `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc`,\n  `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc`,\n  `test/d2_wedge_min_repro.clj`, `test/d2_wedge_probe2.clj`,\n  `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc`,\n  `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`,\n  `test/yin/vm/semantic/derive_test.cljc`,\n  `test/yin/vm/semantic/linearize_test.cljc`.\n  SHA-256 of `git diff` output:\n  `05076f51add1a5b5285c62c6b85c7eb8875d7c2780a7b33613e46742a250887d`.\n- Measurement script SHA-256:\n  `345b432dace388ce20bb463d2241c650b400b644b5194cd0ddae1a3fb42b37c8`.\n- This declaration and the findings are untracked collab files and\n  are not part of the `git diff` digest. Nothing is committed.\n\nV2.1 run: the §4 command exactly as now declared (with\n`:jvm-opts [\"-Xss64m\"]` supplied by `:f6`), 2026-11-11, warm JVM,\nthis host/JVM; run scope\n`cc3-f6-measure-v2-326ca2ee-2f81-4711-9377-42cd2c62e080`;\nafter-release GC-used heap 39,226,944 B; both C lanes `:completed`\nin all 3 pipeline repetitions; the run's `/tmp/cc3-f6-store-*` file\nstores were removed afterwards. All samples recorded; verdicts are\nmaximum-based (§4 rule):\n\n| Quantity | V2.1 samples (all recorded) | Maximum | Ceiling (§3) | Verdict (max rule) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Retained: compiled-inclusive holder (acceptance) | 8,828,592 / 8,832,864 / 8,888,424 / 8,829,928 / 8,924,640 B | 8,924,640 B | 12,000,000 B | PASS (74.4% of ceiling) |\n| Retained: binding-only holder (informational) | 8,203,464 / 7,920,344 / 7,918,160 / 8,014,944 / 7,923,464 B | 8,203,464 B | 12,000,000 B | under (informational; not the acceptance holder) |\n| Storage: rows canonical bytes | 312,886 B ×3 | 312,886 B | 2,000,000 B | PASS |\n| Storage: relation canonical bytes | 856,315 B ×3 | 856,315 B | 2,000,000 B | PASS |\n| Storage: durable record canonical bytes | 544 B ×3 | 544 B | — (in aggregate) | — |\n| Storage: aggregate retained set | 1,169,745 B ×3 | 1,169,745 B | 4,000,000 B | PASS |\n| Peak used heap (2 ms sampling) | 251,948,768 / 272,026,880 / 263,341,656 B | 272,026,880 B | 1,073,741,824 B | PASS |\n| Pipeline elapsed | 772 / 769 / 743 ms | 772 ms | 10,000 ms | PASS |\n\nThe script's printed `:under-ceilings-v2` map was all-true. The\nv2.1 figures sit beside the v2 (r5) figures (compiled-inclusive max\n8,931,952 B without `-Xss64m`; v2.1 max 8,924,640 B with it) — the\nceiling holds under both stack settings, which is why §1 records\n`-Xss64m` as declared parity/headroom rather than a requirement.\nSerialized sizes are unchanged from v2 (the measurement fixture's\nadmission scope is the script's own run scope in both runs).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"ls -ld target/d1* 2>/dev/null; hostname; git rev-parse HEAD; rg -n 'defn.*(kernel-run|kernel-compile|attributed)|defn.*record|defn.*recipe' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj src/cljc/yang/correspondence*.clj*; sed -n '2500,2595p;4473,4547p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; df -h .; date -u '+%F %T'; date '+%F %T %Z'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"ls -ld target/d1* 2>/dev/null; hostname; git rev-parse HEAD; rg -n 'defn.*(kernel-run|kernel-compile|attributed)|defn.*record|defn.*recipe' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj src/cljc/yang/correspondence*.clj*; sed -n '2500,2595p;4473,4547p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; df -h .; date -u '+%F %T'; date '+%F %T %Z'\"","aggregated_output":"jupiter.stigmergy.systems\n747e80fce0428f6971299819b1623b99e01f4bb0\nsrc/cljc/yang/correspondence_verifier.clj:268:(defn attributed?\nsrc/cljc/yang/correspondence_batch.clj:110:(defn record!\nsrc/cljc/yang/correspondence.cljc:33:(defn recipe?\nsrc/cljc/yang/correspondence.cljc:107:(defn store-recipe!\nsrc/cljc/yang/correspondence.cljc:119:(defn store-record!\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1025:(defn- upstream-record-data\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2343:(defn- kernel-record-credits?\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2491:(defn- kernel-compile\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2561:(defn- kernel-compile-in-run\n   admissions through the token, and projected keys (reconstructed\n   from a single-member envelope, member index always zero) agree\n   with the recorded origin for every ordinal. Both coordinates are\n   recorded WHEN ADMITTING, before compilation, validated by the\n   same origin-shape rules as every source origin\n   (`vm/source-origin`), and retained with the compilation as\n   `:admission-origin` plain data. There is no per-JVM global\n   counter (r3 F2) and no default admission stamping every admission\n   alike (r4 F2): every caller supplies its coordinates explicitly,\n   and replay of one retained compilation reuses its recorded\n   coordinate.\"\n  ([fixture admission-scope admission-ordinal]\n   (kernel-compile fixture admission-scope admission-ordinal false))\n  ([fixture admission-scope admission-ordinal retain-input?]\n   (let [coordinate {:fixture (:id fixture) :scope admission-scope :ordinal admission-ordinal}\n         call (kernel-c-program fixture)\n         forms (kernel-closure call)\n         forms-edn (when retain-input?\n                     (correspondence-text/capture! (assoc coordinate :input :forms) forms))\n         call-edn (when retain-input?\n                    (correspondence-text/capture! (assoc coordinate :input :call) call))\n         source-hash (kernel-canonical-source-hash forms call)\n         admission-origin (vm/source-origin\n                            :program [admission-scope admission-ordinal] 0)\n         program (into (into ['(def gate-execution-trace (stream/make 1000000))]\n                             kernel-site-prelude)\n                       (concat (map kernel-trace-form forms) [call]))\n         program (into (yang/library-for program) program)\n         opts (update arg-vector-opts :native into\n                      (map (fn [[op profile]] [(clojure.core/symbol \"stream\" (name op)) profile])\n                           module/stream-profiles))\n         program-edn (when retain-input?\n                       (correspondence-text/capture! (assoc coordinate :input :program) program))\n         options-edn (when retain-input?\n                       (correspondence-text/capture! (assoc coordinate :input :options) opts))\n         compiled (yang/compile-program program true opts)\n         ;; caller-side site ids at the compiled application expressions,\n         ;; post-macroexpansion (R2), with the mechanically derived site\n         ;; table (R7); every assembled definition is instrumented\n         {stamped :ast sites :sites} (kernel-stamp-sites\n                                       compiled (into #{} (map second) forms))\n         missing (unbound-ast-symbols stamped program)]\n     (if (seq missing)\n       {:status :blocked :phase :admission :blocked-by (vec (sort missing))\n        :owners (into {} (for [s missing]\n                           [s (mapv second (filter #(some #{s} (tree-seq coll? seq %)) program))]))}\n       (cond-> {:status :compiled :ast stamped :forms forms :compiled-ast compiled\n                :admission-origin admission-origin\n                :admission-scope admission-scope\n                :admission-ordinal admission-ordinal\n                :site-table (into {} (map (juxt :site identity)) sites)\n                :site-table-hash source-hash\n                :sites sites\n                :canonical-source-hash source-hash}\n         retain-input?\n         (assoc :reconstruction-input\n                {:fixture fixture :forms forms :call call :program program\n                 :program-edn program-edn :forms-edn forms-edn :call-edn call-edn\n                 :options-edn options-edn :options opts :admission-origin admission-origin}))))))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-compile-in-run\n  \"Compile `fixture` as the next admission of `run`: the run's scope\n   with a distinct ordinal assigned by the run composition.\"\n  ([run fixture] (kernel-compile-in-run run fixture false))\n  ([run fixture retain-input?]\n   (kernel-compile fixture (:scope run) (admission-run-ordinal run) retain-input?)))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-c\n  [compiled lane]\n  (if (= :compiled (:status compiled))\n    (assoc (kernel-attempt\n             #(let [machine (compiler-test/run-guest-machine\n                              (:ast compiled) (oracle-registry yang/kind-module) lane 4000000)\n                    v (vm/value machine)\n                    ref (get-in machine [:store 'gate-execution-trace])\n                    handle (get-in machine [:resources (:id ref)])]\n                (when-not (and (vm/halted? machine) handle)\n                  (throw (ex-info \"Execution trace did not complete\" {:lane lane})))\n                {:status :completed :outcome (evidence-data v) :shape (result-shape (evidence-data v))\n                 :executed-calls (tu/drain handle)}))\n           :lane lane)\n    (assoc compiled :lane lane)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Depth harness (max live-K per workload)\n;; =============================================================================\n;;\n;; Measurement only: no admission gate and no correctness assertions. Each\n;; kernel-gate fixture is a workload; the max continuation depth (the semantic\n;; lane's K-vector length, the walker lane's :next chain length) is recorded\n;; per lane. The same instrumentation applies to the pre-port outcome-model\n;; tree and the post-port continuation tree, so the two numbers are directly\n;; comparable.\n(defn- d1-persist-and-check-fixture!\n  \"Exercise one live admission through a temporary file store and the\n   independent static gate; with opts, also run one mutated-input check\n   per distinct gate refusal class. Does not produce a D1 record or a\n   verifier result.\"\n  [dir run fixture & [{:keys [spot-check? handle]}]]\n  (let [compiled (kernel-compile-in-run run fixture true)\n        _ (when-not (= :compiled (:status compiled))\n            (throw (ex-info \"Fixture did not compile\" {:fixture (:id fixture) :stage :compile})))\n        origin (:admission-origin compiled)\n        evidence (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/slice9_site_tables.edn\")))\n        expected (get-in evidence [:fixtures (:id fixture)])\n        _ (when-not (and (= 1 (:version evidence)) (map? expected))\n            (throw (ex-info \"Fixture evidence missing\" {:fixture (:id fixture) :stage :evidence})))\n        producer (cc3-oracle-binding compiled)\n        independent (correspondence-verifier/reconstruct-bindings\n                      (:compiled-ast compiled) (:ast compiled) origin)\n        _ (when-not (= independent (:binding producer))\n            (throw (ex-info \"Independent binding disagreement\" {:fixture (:id fixture) :stage :bindings})))\n        snapshot {:fixture (:id fixture) :origin origin\n                  :bindings independent :metadata (:rows producer)\n                  :constructors (correspondence-verifier/context-constructors context-forms)}\n        own-store? (nil? handle)\n        handle (or handle (file-store/open {:type :file :dir dir}))\n        addresses (try (let [root (vm/materialize-tree! handle (:tree producer))\n                             stamped-root (vm/materialize-tree! handle (:stamped-tree producer))]\n                         {:evidence (correspondence/store-evidence! handle evidence)\n                          :input (jing/materialize! handle (:reconstruction-input compiled))\n                          :profile (jing/materialize! handle correspondence-text/profile)\n                          :snapshot (jing/materialize! handle (assoc snapshot :root root :stamped-root stamped-root))\n                          :root root :stamped-root stamped-root})\n                       (finally (when own-store? (file-store/close! handle))))\n        reopened (if own-store? (file-store/open {:type :file :dir dir}) handle)]\n    (try\n      (let [stored-evidence (jing/get reopened (:evidence addresses) ::missing)\n            stored-input (jing/get reopened (:input addresses) ::missing)\n            stored-snapshot (jing/get reopened (:snapshot addresses) ::missing)\n            stored-profile (jing/get reopened (:profile addresses) ::missing)\n            row (get-in stored-evidence [:fixtures (:id fixture)])\n            before-tree (correspondence-verifier/fetch-tree! reopened (:root stored-snapshot) 100000)\n            stamped-tree (correspondence-verifier/fetch-tree! reopened (:stamped-root stored-snapshot) 100000)\n            input (assoc stored-snapshot\n                         :before (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast before-tree)\n                         :stamped (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast stamped-tree)\n                         :forms (correspondence-text/read-one! (:id fixture) (:forms-edn stored-input))\n                         :call (correspondence-text/read-one! (:id fixture) (:call-edn stored-input))\n                         :source-hash (:canonical-source-hash row)\n                         :site-table (:site-table row))\n            _ (when-not (= correspondence-text/profile stored-profile)\n                (throw (ex-info \"Profile missing or changed\" {:fixture (:id fixture) :stage :profile})))\n            _ (when-not (= (:admission-origin stored-input) (:origin stored-snapshot))\n                (throw (ex-info \"Retained admission differs\" {:fixture (:id fixture) :stage :admission})))\n            replay-program (correspondence-text/read-one! (:id fixture) (:program-edn stored-input))\n            replay-options (correspondence-text/read-one! (:id fixture) (:options-edn stored-input))\n            _ (correspondence-verifier/check-replay-root!\n                (:id fixture) (yang/compile-program replay-program true replay-options) (:root stored-snapshot))\n            gate (correspondence-verifier/check-fixture! input)\n            site-id (first (keys (:site-table row)))\n            _ (when-not site-id\n                (throw (ex-info \"No declaration to mutate\" {:fixture (:id fixture) :stage :mutation})))\n            mutated (assoc-in input [:site-table site-id :arg-shapes] [:forged])\n            mutation (try (correspondence-verifier/check-fixture! mutated) nil\n                          (catch Exception e (ex-data e)))]\n        (when-not (= :site-declarations (:stage mutation))\n          (throw (ex-info \"Mutated declaration was not refused\" {:fixture (:id fixture) :stage :mutation})))\n        {:gate gate :mutation-stage (:stage mutation)\n         :admission-origin (:origin stored-snapshot) :evidence-address (:evidence addresses)\n         :rows {:pre-stamp (count (:rows before-tree))\n                :stamped (count (:rows stamped-tree))}\n         :sites (count (:site-table row))\n         :spot-checks (when spot-check? (d1-spot-check-refusals! input))})\n      (finally (when own-store? (file-store/close! reopened))))))\n\n\n(deftest test-d1-persisted-per-fixture-static-gate\nFilesystem      Size  Used Avail Use% Mounted on\n/dev/nvme0n1p2  938G  331G  559G  38% /home/sto/workspace/datomworld-d1\n2026-11-14 08:04:55\n2026-11-14 03:04:55 EST\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The r8 findings say its measurement store was deleted, and there is no `target/d1-*` store in this checkout. Its outcomes also do not retain the per-fixture input and snapshot addresses, so they cannot themselves supply the persisted record required for the tagged run. I’m checking the available runtime and the record contract before deciding what can be established on this host."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat src/cljc/yang/correspondence.cljc; sed -n '268,350p' src/cljc/yang/correspondence_verifier.clj; rg -n '§4.2|verification-result|verification result|slice9_verification|recipe' docs/design/*correspond* collab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-durable-correspondence.prompt.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat src/cljc/yang/correspondence.cljc; sed -n '268,350p' src/cljc/yang/correspondence_verifier.clj; rg -n '§4.2|verification-result|verification result|slice9_verification|recipe' docs/design/*correspond* collab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-durable-correspondence.prompt.md\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.correspondence\n  \"Structural checks for D1 records. These checks do not establish reliance:\n   all referenced content and relationships still require reconstruction.\"\n  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]))\n\n\n(def ^:private record-keys\n  #{:yang.correspondence/schema :yang.correspondence/evidence\n    :yang.correspondence/recipe :yang.correspondence/inputs\n    :yang.correspondence/roots :yang.correspondence/origin-bindings\n    :yang.correspondence/artifacts :yang.correspondence/metadata\n    :yang.correspondence/instruction-provenance})\n\n\n(def ^:private recipe-keys\n  #{:yang.correspondence.recipe/schema :yang.correspondence.recipe/function\n    :yang.correspondence.recipe/profile :yang.correspondence.recipe/input-roles\n    :yang.correspondence.recipe/evidence-contract :yang.correspondence.recipe/coverage})\n\n\n(defn- distinct-vector?\n  [v pred]\n  (and (vector? v) (every? pred v) (= (count v) (count (set v)))))\n\n\n(defn- role?\n  [entry]\n  (and (vector? entry) (= 2 (count entry)) (keyword? (first entry))\n       (int? (second entry)) (<= 0 (second entry))))\n\n\n(defn recipe?\n  \"Check the closed schema and basic shapes, without resolving the profile.\"\n  [x]\n  (and (map? x) (= recipe-keys (set (keys x)))\n       (= 1 (:yang.correspondence.recipe/schema x))\n       (qualified-symbol? (:yang.correspondence.recipe/function x))\n       (jing/segment-address? (:yang.correspondence.recipe/profile x))\n       (distinct-vector? (:yang.correspondence.recipe/input-roles x) role?)\n       (some? (:yang.correspondence.recipe/evidence-contract x))\n       (jing/segment-address? (:yang.correspondence.recipe/coverage x))))\n\n\n(defn- path-step?\n  [x]\n  (or (and (int? x) (<= 0 x))\n      (and (vector? x) (= 2 (count x))\n           (every? #(and (int? %) (<= 0 %)) x))))\n\n\n(defn- binding?\n  [entry]\n  (and (vector? entry) (= 2 (count entry))\n       (some? (first entry))\n       (let [k (second entry)]\n         (and (vector? k) (= 3 (count k))\n              (vm/occurrence-origin? (nth k 0))\n              (jing/segment-address? (nth k 1))\n              (vector? (nth k 2)) (every? path-step? (nth k 2))))))\n\n\n(defn- artifact?\n  [x]\n  (and (map? x) (= #{:format :identity :storage :derivation} (set (keys x)))\n       (keyword? (:format x)) (some? (:identity x))\n       (jing/segment-address? (:storage x))\n       (jing/segment-address? (:derivation x))))\n\n\n(defn correspondence?\n  \"Check the closed schema and basic shapes, not addresses or endpoints.\n   Compilation-scoped site uniqueness is checked during reconstruction.\"\n  [x]\n  (and (map? x) (= record-keys (set (keys x)))\n       (= 1 (:yang.correspondence/schema x))\n       (every? jing/segment-address?\n               [(:yang.correspondence/evidence x) (:yang.correspondence/recipe x)\n                (:yang.correspondence/metadata x)])\n       (distinct-vector? (:yang.correspondence/inputs x) jing/segment-address?)\n       (distinct-vector? (:yang.correspondence/roots x) jing/segment-address?)\n       (distinct-vector? (:yang.correspondence/artifacts x) artifact?)\n       (distinct-vector? (:yang.correspondence/instruction-provenance x) jing/segment-address?)\n       (distinct-vector? (:yang.correspondence/origin-bindings x) binding?)))\n\n\n(defn store-evidence!\n  \"Store the complete version-1 site-table value without projecting its rows.\n   This checks only the outer version; reconstruction must validate the data.\"\n  [handle evidence]\n  (when-not (and (map? evidence) (= 1 (:version evidence))\n                 (map? (:fixtures evidence)))\n    (throw (ex-info \"Unsupported oracle evidence\" {:rule :correspondence/evidence-schema})))\n  (jing/materialize! handle evidence))\n\n\n(defn- require-content!\n  [handle address]\n  (let [missing ::missing\n        content (jing/get handle address missing)]\n    (when (= missing content)\n      (throw (ex-info \"Correspondence input is missing\"\n                      {:rule :correspondence/missing-content :address address})))\n    content))\n\n\n(defn store-recipe!\n  \"Store a structurally valid recipe after its profile and coverage are present.\n   This is a publication precondition, not interpretation of either object.\"\n  [handle recipe]\n  (when-not (recipe? recipe)\n    (throw (ex-info \"Malformed correspondence recipe\" {:rule :correspondence/recipe})))\n  (doseq [address [(:yang.correspondence.recipe/profile recipe)\n                   (:yang.correspondence.recipe/coverage recipe)]]\n    (require-content! handle address))\n  (jing/materialize! handle recipe))\n\n\n(defn store-record!\n  \"Store a structurally valid correspondence with its direct references present.\n   Checks declared roots and markers, but not paths, transitive closures,\n   derivations, or attribution.\"\n  [handle record]\n  (when-not (correspondence? record)\n    (throw (ex-info \"Malformed correspondence\" {:rule :correspondence/record})))\n  (let [recipe (require-content! handle (:yang.correspondence/recipe record))\n        inputs (:yang.correspondence/inputs record)]\n    (when-not (recipe? recipe)\n      (throw (ex-info \"Malformed correspondence recipe\" {:rule :correspondence/recipe})))\n    (let [evidence (require-content! handle (:yang.correspondence/evidence record))\n          coverage (require-content! handle (:yang.correspondence.recipe/coverage recipe))]\n      (when-not (and (= [:slice9-site-tables 1] (:yang.correspondence.recipe/evidence-contract recipe))\n                     (map? evidence) (= 1 (:version evidence)) (map? (:fixtures evidence)))\n        (throw (ex-info \"Unsupported oracle evidence contract\"\n                        {:rule :correspondence/evidence-schema})))\n      (when (and (or (empty? (:yang.correspondence/artifacts record))\n                     (empty? (:yang.correspondence/instruction-provenance record)))\n                 (not= :tree-only (:scope coverage)))\n        (throw (ex-info \"Empty image claims require tree-only coverage\"\n                        {:rule :correspondence/coverage}))))\n    (doseq [[_ index] (:yang.correspondence.recipe/input-roles recipe)]\n      (when-not (< index (count inputs))\n        (throw (ex-info \"Recipe input is absent\" {:rule :correspondence/input-role :index index}))))\n    (doseq [address (concat [(:yang.correspondence/evidence record)\n                             (:yang.correspondence.recipe/profile recipe)\n                             (:yang.correspondence.recipe/coverage recipe)\n                             (:yang.correspondence/metadata record)]\n                            inputs\n                            (:yang.correspondence/roots record)\n                            (:yang.correspondence/instruction-provenance record)\n                            (mapcat (juxt :storage :derivation)\n                                    (:yang.correspondence/artifacts record)))]\n      (require-content! handle address))\n    (let [metadata (require-content! handle (:yang.correspondence/metadata record))\n          roots (set (:yang.correspondence/roots record))\n          marker-counts (frequencies metadata)]\n      (when-not (vector? metadata)\n        (throw (ex-info \"Malformed frontend metadata\" {:rule :correspondence/metadata})))\n      (doseq [[_ [origin root path]] (:yang.correspondence/origin-bindings record)]\n        (when-not (and (contains? roots root)\n                       (= 1 (get marker-counts [origin root path :yang/call-site 1])))\n          (throw (ex-info \"Binding has no declared root and unique marker\"\n                          {:rule :correspondence/binding-endpoint})))))\n    (jing/materialize! handle record)))\n\n\n(defn binding-coverage?\n  \"Check one compilation's site and marker relations against its row tree.\n   This does not reconstruct the binding or independently derive site classes.\"\n  [site-table origin tree metadata bindings]\n  (and (map? site-table) (vm/occurrence-origin? origin)\n       (map? tree) (vector? metadata) (vector? bindings)\n       (every? #(and (vector? %) (= 5 (count %))) metadata)\n       (distinct-vector? bindings binding?)\n       (let [markers (filterv #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3)) metadata)\n             keys-of (mapv #(subvec % 0 3) markers)\n             eligible (into #{} (map (fn [[root path]] [origin root path]))\n                            (vm/application-occurrences tree))\n             ids (mapv first bindings)\n             targets (mapv second bindings)]\n         (and (every? #(= 1 (nth % 4)) markers)\n              (= (count keys-of) (count (set keys-of)))\n              (= eligible (set keys-of))\n              (= (count ids) (count (set ids)))\n              (= (count targets) (count (set targets)))\n              (= (set ids) (set (keys site-table)))\n              (every? eligible targets)))))\n(defn attributed?\n  \"Query one already-scoped fixture's table, bindings and complete lane traces.\n   This query does not validate those inputs or authorize reliance on them.\"\n  [{:keys [site-table bindings lanes origin root guest-symbol requested-arity carriers]}]\n  (letfn [(eligible?\n            [entry]\n            (when (and (vector? entry) (= 3 (count entry)))\n              (let [[function arity site] entry\n                    row (get site-table site)\n                    key (get bindings site)]\n                (and row (= site (:site row)) (vector? key) (= 3 (count key))\n                     (vm/occurrence-origin? origin) (= origin (first key))\n                     (jing/segment-address? root) (= root (second key)) (vector? (nth key 2))\n                     (not= :gate-site/none site)\n                     (or (and (= function guest-symbol) (= arity requested-arity))\n                         (some (fn [[carrier carrier-arity mode]]\n                                 (and (contains? #{:ambient-delegation :context-shift :context-copy} mode)\n                                      (= function carrier) (= arity carrier-arity)\n                                      (= carrier (:callee row)) (not (:delegation? row))\n                                      (or (not= :ambient-delegation mode)\n                                          (= :ambient-literal (first (:arg-shapes row))))))\n                               carriers))))))]\n    (every? (fn [lane-id]\n              (let [lane (get lanes lane-id)]\n                (and (= :completed (:status lane)) (true? (:complete? lane))\n                     (some eligible? (:executed-calls lane)))))\n            [:c-walker :c-semantic])))\n\n\n(defn check-fixture!\n  \"Run independent static checks for one supplied compilation. This does not\n   establish admission authenticity, executable-image derivations, trace\n   completeness, durable retrieval, or D1 reliance.\"\n  [{:keys [fixture before stamped origin constructors forms call source-hash\n           site-table bindings metadata]}]\n  (letfn [(require!\n            [condition stage]\n            (when-not condition\n              (throw (ex-info \"Independent fixture check refused\"\n                              {:rule :verifier/fixture :fixture fixture :stage stage}))))]\n    (require! (and fixture (vm/occurrence-origin? origin) (map? before)\n                   (map? stamped) (set? constructors) (some? forms) (some? call)\n                   (string? source-hash) (map? site-table) (map? bindings)\n                   (vector? metadata)) :inputs)\n    (let [actual-hash (try (yang.correspondence-verifier/source-hash forms call)\n                           (catch Exception e\n                             (throw (ex-info \"Source hash reconstruction failed\"\n                                             {:rule :verifier/fixture :fixture fixture :stage :source-hash} e))))]\n      (require! (= source-hash actual-hash) :source-hash))\n    (let [actual-sites (try (site-declarations stamped constructors)\n                            (catch Exception e\n                              (throw (ex-info \"Site reconstruction failed\"\n                                              {:rule :verifier/fixture :fixture fixture :stage :site-declarations} e))))]\n      (require! (= site-table actual-sites) :site-declarations))\n    (let [actual-bindings (try (reconstruct-bindings before stamped origin)\n                               (catch Exception e\n                                 (throw (ex-info \"Binding reconstruction failed\"\n                                                 {:rule :verifier/fixture :fixture fixture :stage :bindings} e))))]\n      (require! (= bindings actual-bindings) :bindings))\n    (let [tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode before)\n          markers (filterv #(and (vector? %) (= 5 (count %))\n                                 (= :yang/call-site (nth % 3))) metadata)\n          keys (mapv #(subvec % 0 3) markers)\n          expected (into #{} (map (fn [[root path]] [origin root path]))\n                         (vm/application-occurrences tree))]\n      (require! (and (nil? (vm/validate-rows tree))\n                     (every? #(and (vector? %) (= 5 (count %))) metadata)\n                     (every? #(= 1 (nth % 4)) markers)\n                     (= (count keys) (count (set keys)))\n                     (= expected (set keys))) :metadata))\n    {:fixture fixture :status :static-pass}))\n\n\n(defn fetch-tree!\n  \"Fetch a bounded complete canonical row closure; refuse missing or invalid rows.\"\n  [handle root max-rows]\n  (when-not (and (jing/segment-address? root) (integer? max-rows) (pos? max-rows))\n    (throw (ex-info \"Invalid row retrieval request\" {:rule :verifier/tree-request})))\n  (loop [pending [root] rows {}]\n    (if-let [address (peek pending)]\n      (if (contains? rows address)\n        (recur (pop pending) rows)\n        (do\nrg: docs/design/*correspond*: No such file or directory (os error 2)\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-durable-correspondence.prompt.md:22:- `collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md` §4 (the D1 envelope, verbatim-evidence rule, the recipe, independent reconstruction), §6.3 (bounds), §8 (acceptance sequence).\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-durable-correspondence.prompt.md:29:1. **The D1 envelope** — `:yang.correspondence/schema 1` per design §4.1: closed key set; `:evidence` names the v1 tables VERBATIM (address, never a copy); `:recipe`; `:inputs` (retrievable closures, not commit strings); `:roots`; `:origin-bindings` (evidence-local site id → persisted K, unique within the claimed compilation, endpoints validated); `:artifacts`; `:metadata` (the C1 rows' address); `:instruction-provenance`. Content-addressed via dao.jing; no self-address field.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-durable-correspondence.prompt.md:30:2. **The recipe record** — `:yang.correspondence.recipe/schema 1` per design §4.1: closed, versioned, naming the interpreter function, the exact reconstruction profile (frontend revision, grammar/options, expansion environment, recorded origins/attempts, transformations, canonicalization, site-table derivation, lowering rules), input roles, and the oracle's exact schema identity.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-durable-correspondence.prompt.md:32:4. **The independent reconstruction verifier** — per design §4.2's seven steps and the mob's Q1 conditions: verify addresses and schemas; verify each code image under its own execution contract; reconstruct the compilation under the exact recipe; re-derive the oracle site declarations from compiled AST argument expressions (not from the producer's serialized classifications); reconstruct every claimed binding with exact coverage and multiplicities; execute the attribution query over separately scoped relations; publish a separate verification result naming the verifier revision. **The verifier must not call the producer's derivation as its only check** (design §4.2's explicit warning about `latte_oracle_tables.clj`).\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-durable-correspondence.prompt.md:38:MAY edit: `src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj`, `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`, the new companion file + its validator, `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc` (only if a side-artifact handle is missing), and NEW files for the record/recipe/verifier under `src/cljc/yang/` (propose exact paths in findings).\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
